The Company:

&nbsp;

VeSync is a portfolio company with brands that cover different categories of health &amp; wellness products. We wouldn&rsquo;t be surprised if you have one of our Levoit air purifiers in your living room or a COSORI air fryer whipping up healthy and delicious meals for you every night.

&nbsp;

We&rsquo;re a young and energetic company, we&rsquo;ve had tremendous success, and we are constantly growing our team. As we garner more industry attention - just check out our accomplishments and awards by CES Innovation, iF Design, IGA, and Red Dot - we also need driven and talented people to join our team.

&nbsp;

That brings us to you, and what you&rsquo;ll be joining. Our teams are smart and diligent and take ownership of their work - they&rsquo;re confident in their work but know how to collaborate with open ears and a spirit of learning. If you&rsquo;re down-to-earth, approachable, and easy to strike up a conversation with, this may be a great fit for you.

&nbsp;

Check out our brands:

levoit.com&nbsp;|&nbsp;cosori.com&nbsp;|&nbsp;etekcity.com|&nbsp;pawsync.com

&nbsp;

The Opportunity:

&nbsp;

We&rsquo;re looking for a Senior Product Designer to craft intuitive, scalable, and human-centered experiences across mobile, web, and wearable platforms. In this role, you&rsquo;ll own the end-to-end design process&amp;mdash;from research and concept development through launch&amp;mdash;translating insights into elegant, accessible interfaces that bring our product vision to life.

&nbsp;

You&rsquo;ll establish and evolve design systems that enable consistency and efficiency, partner closely with cross-functional teams to align usability with business goals, and champion design excellence across the organization. This role is ideal for a seasoned designer who thrives in collaboration, obsesses over detail and craft, and is passionate about creating technology that empowers healthier, more meaningful experiences.

&nbsp;

Applicants must include a portfolio of their work when applying.

&nbsp;

What you will do at VeSync:

&nbsp;

1. End-to-End Product Design

• Drive the design of user flows, interfaces, and interactions across app, wearable, and web platforms.

• Own the user experience design from discovery through launch.

• Translate user insights, research findings, and product strategy into intuitive, engaging, and scalable interfaces.

• Partner with Product Managers, Engineers, and Researchers to ensure design decisions balance value, usability, feasibility, and viability.

• Deliver design assets that reflect clarity, accessibility, and brand consistency.

• Rapidly prototype and iterate concepts using real user feedback and data.

&nbsp;

2. Design Systems &amp; Scalable Practices

• Establish scalable patterns, components, and reusable assets to accelerate design execution.

• Improve design tooling, documentation, and workflows to support team efficiency.

• Define and document design principles that reflect the brand,

1.Develop visual assets for overseas markets （ North America, Southeast Asia), including digital campaigns, social media content, marketing materials, and in-store visuals;


2.Participate in campaign ideation and execution, ensuring strong and consistent brand visual identity;


3.Localize visual content based on cultural context across different regions to enhance engagement and effectiveness;


4.Collaborate closely with brand, marketing, PR, and local teams to support product launches, seasonal campaigns, and brand collaborations;


5.Establish and maintain overseas visual guidelines to ensure consistency across channels;


6.Stay updated on design trends and competitive landscape to continuously elevate brand aesthetics.


Qualifications：


1.Bachelor’s degree or above in Graphic Design, Visual Communication, Digital Media, or related fields;


2.Minimum 3 years of experience in visual design, with life-style brand-side experience preferred;


3.Strong sense of branding and aesthetics, with proven experience in end-to-end visual projects;


4.Proficient in design tools (e.g., Adobe Creative Suite); motion or video skills are a plus;


5.Strong cross-cultural awareness; overseas project experience is a plus;


6.Fluent in English (both written and spoken) as a working language;


7.Strong communication and collaboration skills, with the ability to work across time zones.

UX Designer&nbsp;


Do you want to work on leading edge technology? Are you ready to build products that revolutionize history? At Intrinsic you will! We are a modern software development company creating new product solutions across a variety of industries. We build the latest web applications, cloud microservice architectures, and modern simulation technology applications. Send us your info and let us discuss the opportunity!&nbsp;


Job Description:&nbsp;
Intrinsic is looking for a skilled and self-motivated UX Designer that is passionate about building new products and loves to exceed the expectations of customers. As a UX Designer you will help us identify and implement new and exciting UX features to deliver to our customers and bring our products to the next level! Please note that this posting is intended to identify qualified individuals for an upcoming contract opportunity. Employment is contingent upon contract award.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
As a team member, you will:&nbsp;

- Drive collaborations between the development and business teams to draft, prototype, and realize design solutions&nbsp;
- Participate in team agile ceremonies and sprints&nbsp;
- Work closely with the Intrinsic Product Director, Chief Technology Officer, and team Scrum Master to assure the platform is being delivered on time and exceeding client expectations&nbsp;
- Be a passionate advocate for the user and translate their feedback into design features and solutions&nbsp;
- Assure team cohesiveness in a “leadership by example” approach, building high-quality product features that exceed client expectations&nbsp;
- Design, build, and push a new product to an emerging marketspace&nbsp;


Work on a dynamic, adaptable, and high performing team helping the UX process for Intrinsic’s core capabilities:&nbsp;

- Modern Software Engineering&nbsp;
- Customized AI/ML&nbsp;
- Operational and Simulated Training&nbsp;
- Enterprise Cloud and Offline Environments&nbsp;
- AR/VR and Live Virtual Constructive Simulation&nbsp;
- Product Development with UX/UI Prototyping&nbsp;
- Big Data Analytics&nbsp;


Minimum qualifications:&nbsp;

- Bachelor's degree in Design, Human Computer Interaction, or equivalent experience&nbsp;
- 2+ years of relevant experience on a diverse software development team&nbsp;
- 2+ years of experience working in Agile delivery environments&nbsp;
- Experience designing wire frames, prototypes, and high-fidelity front-end designs for intuitive user interaction&nbsp;
- 1+ year of experience with web environments such as HTML, CSS, JavaScript&nbsp;
- 1+ years of experience with industry tools such as Sketch, InVision, Figma, Adobe Illustrator, Miro&nbsp;


Preferred qualifications:&nbsp;

- Experience building and shipping products&nbsp;
- Experience working with the DoD, large aerospace enterprise, or AI/ML industry&nbsp;
- 3+ years in production and operations on consumer digital products&nbsp;
- 3+ years of experience in UX design&nbsp;
- 3+ years of project manageme

