The Opportunity:

&nbsp;

As a Senior Visual Designer, you will lead the design and optimization of high-impact digital experiences and marketing assets that drive measurable results. You will take a lead role in designing websites, landing pages, mobile apps, emails, and digital ads, ensuring every deliverable is elevated by sophisticated design and aligned with established brand standards.

&nbsp;

This role requires an expert-level command of design fundamentals and a deep understanding of how visual hierarchy impacts user experience and conversion. Beyond execution, you will act as a design lead on key projects, collaborating cross-functionally with marketing and product teams to translate business goals into compelling visual solutions while maintaining the integrity of our design systems.

&nbsp;

&nbsp;


What you will do at VeSync:


- High-Impact Design Execution: Lead the design and optimization of websites, landing pages, mobile experiences, and digital ads, ensuring a high bar for both visual craft and performance.

- Design System Stewardship: Maintain and expand existing design systems, including style guides, UI kits, and typography standards, to ensure brand consistency across all digital platforms.

- Prototyping &amp; Collaboration: Develop responsive, high-fidelity prototypes in Figma to clearly communicate complex interactions to stakeholders and developers.

- Cross-Functional Partnership: Work closely with marketing and product teams to translate campaign objectives into effective, visually compelling creative assets.

- Performance Optimization: Use data from A/B testing and user analytics to proactively refine designs, focusing on improving engagement and conversion rates.

- Design Quality Control: Ensure all outputs are user-friendly, technically sound, and aligned with the strategic goals of the marketing team.

- Trend Integration

Graphic Designer - Men's Apparel


About the Position:&nbsp;
As our apparel business continues to grow, we’re expanding our team! We’re seeking a Men’s Apparel Graphic Designer with strong communication skills, excellent attention to detail, and hands-on experience. The ideal candidate is self-motivated, organized, proactive, and thrives in a fast-paced environment—with the ability to multi-task and prioritize responsibilities to ensure every customer and order receives exceptional support and accuracy. Assisting the design team to drive the development of color, material, and graphic direction for seasonal product categories.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Responsibilities:&nbsp;
- Men’s Design Department graphic design support- with cooperation from Art Department&nbsp;
- Demonstrate strong teamwork skills through cooperating with cross-functional team members&nbsp;
- Communications with on site design team as well as global team&nbsp;
- Packaging Development and layout to be printer ready&nbsp;
- Print &amp; graphic art development- to include T-shirts and clothing design elements&nbsp;
- Print &amp; artwork follow up between design and vendors&nbsp;
- Tracking, updating and creating material items using PLM platform&nbsp;
- Misc. graphic support ie: making presentation boards, mocking up hangtags &amp; any in house graphic needs&nbsp;
- Support VP of Men’s Design on Artwork comments and approvals&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Qualifications:&nbsp;
- Bachelor’s degree in Graphic Design with a good understanding of Fashion Design&nbsp;
- Minimum 3+ years of graphic design experience in apparel or a related field&nbsp;
- Experience in Men's Apparel preferred&nbsp;
- Proficient in Adobe suite: Illustrator, Photoshop&nbsp;
- Understanding of screen-printing processes, separations, and graphic production workflows&nbsp;
- Fast paced graphic design workload, able to work under tight deadlines and time constraints&nbsp;
- Strong multi-tasking, communication and organization qualities are a must&nbsp;
- Ability to establish, communicate and maintain effective relationships with all design departments&nbsp;
- Excellent time management and the ability to independently manage multiple projects&nbsp;
- Experience creating licensed graphics a plus&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Hourly Rate $25-$33
Onsite role in Montebello, CA
